L564: Preview Preview abstract We study differentially private k-mean/median clustering in the online streaming setting where a point arrive at each time step and we need to output a set of k centers that optimize the k-mean/median objective of all the points so far. We give a generic transformation that turns the sensitive stream into a differentially private stream, which is a semi-coreset of the original stream and allows us to run any (non-private) online clustering algorithm as a post-processing step.
L565: Our algorithm is efficient in terms of errors, space and running time compared to existing algorithms (Epasto et al., 2023; Dupr{\'{e}} la Tour, 2024). Furthermore, our reduction allows us to inherit properties of the non-private clustering, such as consistency (Lattanzi and Vassilvitski, 2017), which was not satisfied by previous DP algorithms. cite60†View details L566: cite66†Towards AI as a Collaborative Partner: A Taxonomy of AI Agent Behavior in Software Engineering L567: 
